    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe change harness committed run records only locally. Opening an implementation PR left plans, reports, evidence and allocation reservations unavailable on the remote, and interruption could leave publication status unclear.\n\n## What changes\n\nThe harness now publishes each authoritative artifact checkpoint to the separate orphan `origin/harness-artifacts` branch with a non-force push and independent remote-ref verification. It binds the destination, supports explicit adoption of reviewed existing history, preserves local checkpoints after failures, and blocks forward work until publication is reconciled.\n\nTerminal state and the cleared active pointer are published in one final checkpoint. Recovery verifies or retries that checkpoint without repeating accepted implementation or creating another PR. FOS-000027 completion bookkeeping is included in this reviewed source branch.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nRun evidence and permanent allocation records remain available remotely alongside the proposed implementation, with an honest distinction between local commits and confirmed publication.\n\n## Why this approach\n\nThe committed Git ref remains authoritative. Publication derives confirmation from the actual remote instead of creating commits acknowledging themselves. Conservative handling of remote advances and divergence preserves both writers' records and requires explicit reconciliation when run state has evolved. The local lock coordinates worktrees on one machine; distributed ownership remains separately coordinated.\n\n## Verification and limits\n\nIndependent unit, bookkeeping-renewal and separate final reviews passed all 51 Python/Git tests without skips, plus skill metadata validation and original-criteria review. Tests use real disposable bare remotes and clones for publication, rejection, endpoint binding, competing history, interruption and terminal recovery. The independently found historical-reservation-loss defect was fixed and checked against its original counterexample. Existing artifact history was published and its remote SHA verified; terminal checkpoint confirmation follows PR attachment.\n\nNo Fossilize C++, GPU, Steam or hosted-CI verification is claimed. Existing history receives a structural and semantic privacy review before first publication. Artifact history stays separate from this source PR; the harness does not merge the PR.\n\n## Task references\n\n[FOS-000027 \u2014 Commit and publish harness artifacts to the remote orphan branch](https://github.com/robinwassen/Fossilize/blob/codex/FOS-000027-artifact-publication/local-docs/reviews/harness-backlog.md#fos-000027--commit-and-publish-harness-artifacts-to-the-remote-orphan-branch).\n",
